Chapter: LinearCaptureArg
  cites Foreword chapter Linear

 Stage 4 guard: a closure that captures a linear value and escapes as
 a function argument may be invoked any number of times by the
 callee - the capture is rejected (CDX2067). Bind the closure with
 let instead; a let-bound capturing closure is call-once.

Section: Definitions

  apply-twice : (Integer -> Integer), Integer -> Integer
  apply-twice (f) (x) = f (f x)

  spend : linear Integer -> Integer
  spend (n) = apply-twice (\x -> n + x) 1

  opening : Text = show (spend 10)

